<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Uqba ibn Nafi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 622–683</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Okba ibn Nafi, Sidi Okba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Uqba ibn Nafi was an Arab general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun</a> and Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphates</a> who led the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. He founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kairouan">Kairouan</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifriqiya">Ifriqiya</a> around 670 as a base for campaigns against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berbers</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a>, and in a later expedition reportedly reached the Atlantic coast. Returning eastwards, he was ambushed and killed near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biskra">Biskra</a> in 682 or 683 by the Berber leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kusaila">Kusaila</a>; his tomb lies at Sidi Okba in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/uqba-ibn-nafi.jpg" alt="Uqba ibn Nafi" width="320" height="491" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Al hilali al sulaymi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_de_Okba_ibn_Nafi_al_Fihri_en_Alg%C3%A9rie.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
